<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Þorgeir Ljósvetningagoði</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 985–1001</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Thorgeir Ljosvetningagodi, Þorgeir Þorkelsson</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Þorgeir Ljósvetningagoði was a pagan chieftain and the lawspeaker of the Icelandic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/althing">Althing</a> from 985 to 1001. At the Althing of 999 or 1000, chosen to settle the dispute between pagans and Christians, he lay under a cloak for a day and then ruled that all Icelanders should accept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>, while some pagan practices were tolerated in private.</p></div>
